      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm an artist, IMO pens have needed to be a system-level feature for ages now. Relying on world or avatar authors to add pens isn't enough: some worlds have only one or two pens total (a pain if more than one person wants to draw), some pens have very limited stroke resolution/stroke counts (\"oh, the earlier strokes from this drawing are gone\"), and most of them don't reliably sync for people who join late.\n\nThat's to say nothing of the times I join a meetup in a world without pens at all -- it removes one of my main verbs, the thing I do while socializing (in and out of VR), and that makes it hard to justify visiting most worlds for more than a few minutes. Incorporating just a basic single-color world-writing pen as a standardized feature has the potential to solve all these issues.\n\n(Bonuses attached to this, like flashy pen effects and persistent online storage for drawings, can also be nice value-adds for VRChat+, just saying.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
