      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The ability to save pen drawing info that accumulates in a world over the course of a session (far too large for world persistence) would make VR Chat the best 3D Markup Tool for things like (IRL) Architectural Visualization. Much more developed and refined than literally any other product that has ever been marketed at us for this purpose simply because VRChat already has the “VR” part figured out and substantially developed far beyond the gimmick phase that other VR markup tools are stuck in. Making Pens into a system feature instead of a third party prefab is the only way to make this a possibility since this would require sending data out of the World. It makes sense that VRChat might host that 3D pen info on a cloud and monetize access to the “Pen Data Persistence Service” similar to other things that are familiar to AEC industry such as Matterport, so that users can access and import the session pen data into BIM/Architecture software like Revit or as 3D elements into AutoCAD or other things. From experience, I can tell you that a hypothetical plugin for getting cloud-hosted VRC Pen Data into Autodesk Revit would be easy enough that the Revit/Dynamo/BIM community would likely just make a Revit plugin for it, provided that the World Session VRC Pen data from a cloud source were to be a real thing. But the option to save Session Pen Data like this for any use case (not just Architecture) could represent an entire new revenue-source for VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
